From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_SPARE_FRAMES=<K>: while nothing is refused, the out-of-memory collector spares images used in the last K frames (ASTC 2K); EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_MARGIN_MAX_MIB; EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_COUNT line; unset as before

T179a. In the area past the field the pool's largest block stays at 20-44 MiB whatever the collector
frees, so the Vulkan port's PoolPressure() is 2 every frame and the collector runs its aggressive
pass every frame: every image unused for 10 frames goes, ASTC included, and is made, uploaded and
decoded again a few frames later (about 5 deletes and 5 creations a frame, 2.2 of them ASTC, at
~15 fps). Deleting frees space inside VMA blocks (slack), not pool.

EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_SPARE_FRAMES=<K> (1..3600): while no refusal was seen for 600 frames (allocator
MemoryRefusalEvents, the driver's graphics_refusals via the front's weak eden_graphics_refusals, an
image left out) and the images are under the expected mark, every collector pass takes only images
unused for K frames, ASTC only after 2K, and among candidates those unused max(120, 2K) frames go
first. A refusal turns it off for 600 frames, starting with that frame's pass. Other paths
(CollectForBuffer, RefusalEvict, AreaEvict, stale targets, the old pass) unchanged. The pinned GC
anchors of prepare-vulkan-port.py are untouched (no new "Configure(" text, the two pass lines kept).
EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_MARGIN_MAX_MIB=<N> (1..3072): caps "keeping N MiB more free" (log only under the
EDEN_NX2_TC_*_MIB overrides). EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_COUNT=1: the count line only. Line (with
EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG) every 600 frames: "EDEN_UP_TC_OOM 600 frames: ...". All unset: exactly as before.
texture_cache*.h are not translation id inputs and no name is added to TranslationSwitches:
KEEPS THE STORE.

